---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Deliberately selected, published writing. These links ship in the HTML even
// when the sibling site is unavailable during a build. Use its clean URLs.
const writing = [
  {
    title: 'How I use AI',
    href: 'https://probablyfine.dev/blog/how-i-use-ai',
    description: "What I ask the tools to do, what I review, and what I'm responsible for when it ships.",
  },
  {
    title: 'I built dnsweaver because I was tired of managing DNS by hand',
    href: 'https://probablyfine.dev/blog/why-i-built-dnsweaver',
    description: 'The problem in my own lab that became an open-source project.',
  },
  {
    title: 'I just wanted to play games',
    href: 'https://probablyfine.dev/blog/i-just-wanted-to-play-games',
    description: 'Playing DOS games beside my mom, learning to fix my own computers, and finding my way into this work.',
  },
];
---

<Layout>
  <section class="portfolio-intro page-shell" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Solutions &amp; infrastructure architect</p>
      <h1 id="intro-title">I design enterprise infrastructure, argue for it, and then run it.</h1>
      <p class="intro-copy">I'm Maxfield Allison. I've spent ten years working with enterprise customers, and I'm now the application owner and global escalation point for an Azure platform serving thousands of devices across four regions.</p>
      <div class="intro-links">
        <a href="/resume" data-track="cta-resume" class="primary-link">Read my resume <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/about">More about me <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="intro-aside" aria-label="Outside work">
      <p class="eyebrow">Outside work</p>
      <p>I still spend a lot of my free time on computers. The homelab, the open-source projects, and the writing at probablyfine.dev all come out of that. I'd be doing this even if it never helped my career.</p>
      <a href="https://probablyfine.dev/blog?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=portfolio" data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">Visit probablyfine.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="work-title">Some of the work</h2>
      <p>The decisions behind a few projects, including the work it took to get a design approved.</p>
    </div>
    <article class="work-example">
      <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise architecture</p>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="/projects/test-environment" data-track="case-study-test-environment">Making the case for a test environment</a></h3>
        <p>A global platform needed somewhere to test changes. I made the business case, won the funding, and defined the design and sizing across three organizations. The platform teams own the provisioning.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="work-example">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source</p>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="/projects/dnsweaver" data-track="case-study-dnsweaver">Keeping DNS in step with the infrastructure</a></h3>
        <p>dnsweaver started with the records I was tired of maintaining by hand. I own its design, releases, and acceptance criteria. AI agents implement the code.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="work-example">
      <p class="eyebrow">Upstream contribution</p>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="/projects/opnsense-frr" data-track="case-study-opnsense-frr">Picking up an OPNsense issue a bot had closed</a></h3>
        <p>The BGP setting I needed wasn't exposed in the interface. The case study follows the issue through to a contribution merged upstream.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <p class="section-more"><a href="/projects">All case studies <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="writing-title">Writing at probablyfine.dev</h2>
      <p>I write about the projects and the things that got me interested in them. These are a few places to start.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="writing-list">
      {writing.map((post) => (
        <li>
          <h3><a href={`${post.href}?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=selected-writing`} data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">{post.title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3>
          <p>{post.description}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
